course: dictionary
lesson: 6021
title: Mediterranean: a sea, a place, a climate
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Mediterranean starts with a capital M, because it is the name of a sea: the Mediterranean. It can also be a describing word that means of or near that sea. «Mediterranean countries include Spain, France, Italy, Greece, Turkey and Egypt.» Here the word tells you which countries you mean.
explain: Read the words around it to find out which meaning you need. «The Mediterranean is an almost closed sea» is about the sea itself, so it is a noun. «A Mediterranean climate has hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters» describes the weather, so it is an adjective. The clues are the words after it.
explain: Test your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Could you say «a climate of or near the sea» and still make sense? Yes, so Mediterranean means of or near that sea. This check works for almost any new word.
fact: The Mediterranean is a large sea between southern Europe, North Africa and western Asia.
fact: «Mediterranean» means of or near this sea, as in «Mediterranean countries».
fact: A Mediterranean climate has hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters.
fact: Places with a Mediterranean climate include parts of California and Australia, as well as the lands around the sea.
fact: «The Mediterranean is an almost closed sea, and more water evaporates from it than rivers and rain bring in.» Ocean water flows in from the Atlantic to fill it up.
exercise: «The Mediterranean is an almost closed sea.» In this sentence, what is the Mediterranean? | A type of weather | A country | *A sea | A kind of food
exercise: «Mediterranean countries include Spain, France, Italy, Greece, Turkey and Egypt.» What does Mediterranean describe here? | *Countries of or near that sea | Countries where people only speak English | Countries that are all islands | Countries with very tall mountains
exercise: «A Mediterranean climate has hot, dry summers and mild, wet winters.» What are the summers like in a Mediterranean climate? | Cold and snowy | *Hot and dry | Misty and grey | Wet every single day
test: What is the Mediterranean? | A river that flows into Spain | A kind of olive oil | A mountain range in Italy | *A large sea between southern Europe, North Africa and western Asia
test: «To sail from the Mediterranean to Lisbon, a ship passes through the Strait of Gibraltar.» Where does the ship pass on its way to Lisbon? | The Suez Canal | The English Channel | The Panama Canal | *The Strait of Gibraltar
exam: A «Mediterranean diet» means lots of vegetables, fish, olive oil and grains. In this phrase, what does Mediterranean mean? | A type of fast food | *Of or typical of the area around the Mediterranean Sea | Very spicy | Made of metal
